course: dictionary
lesson: 13406
title: Hereinafter: a word for formal papers
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words live mostly in one kind of writing. Hereinafter is found in legal papers, contracts and very formal documents, not in stories or chatty messages.
explain: It means "from this point on in this document" or "later in this text". Read «John Smith (hereinafter called "the Buyer")». The writer is saying that from now on, the Buyer is the short name for John Smith.
explain: Context helps again. The brackets and the word called tell you a short name is coming. Try your meaning in the sentence: "John Smith (from now on called 'the Buyer')" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Hereinafter means from this point on in this document.
fact: «This contract is between Sam Patel (hereinafter "the Seller") and Lily Ross (hereinafter "the Buyer").»
fact: Hereinafter is an adverb. It tells the reader when the short name starts to be used.
fact: Another phrase you may see is «hereinafter referred to as», which means exactly the same thing.
fact: Clue to look for: brackets with a name in quotation marks, such as ("the Club").
exercise: «The school trip form is below (hereinafter "the Form"). Please sign it.» What does hereinafter mean here? | In a different town | Before this point in time | Only once, and never again | *From this point on in this document
exercise: Which word tells the reader that a short name will be used from now on? | Under | *Hereinafter | Football | Yesterday
exercise: «Ms Hale (hereinafter "the Tenant") agrees to keep the flat clean.» Who is the Tenant? | The flat itself | A bus driver | The landlord's dog | *Ms Hale, the person named in the sentence
test: Hereinafter is most likely to be found in which kind of text? | A comic book | A birthday card | *A legal contract | A football match report
test: «The Club agrees to pay the fee (hereinafter "the Club Rules").» What does hereinafter tell the reader? | That the story is funny | *That a shorter name is used from now on | That something happened yesterday | That the text has ended
exam: «Mr Khan (hereinafter "the Owner") must repair the gate.» In this sentence, hereinafter means | *From this point on, a short name will be used | A long time ago | In the garden | After the gate is painted
